  read_url_content {
    url: "https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/"
    web_document {
      document_id: "https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/"
      url: "https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/"
      title: "Introduction | Changelly Exchange API v2"
      timestamp {
        seconds: 1779208488
        nanos: 23176097
      }
      chunks {
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Introduction | Changelly Exchange API v2"
          }
          text: "[Skip to main content](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#__docusaurus_skipToContent_fallback)\n[Changelly Exchange API](https://docs.changelly.com/)\n- [Introduction](https://docs.changelly.com/)\n- [Usage](https://docs.changelly.com/category/usage)\n- [FAQ](https://docs.changelly.com/faq)\n- [Development](https://docs.changelly.com/category/development)\n- [Exchange API reference](https://docs.changelly.com/category/exchange-api-reference)\n- [Migration from Exchange API v1](https://docs.changelly.com/migration-guide)\n[Introduction](https://docs.changelly.com/)\n[Usage](https://docs.changelly.com/category/usage)\n[FAQ](https://docs.changelly.com/faq)\n[Development](https://docs.changelly.com/category/development)\n[Exchange API reference](https://docs.changelly.com/category/exchange-api-reference)\n[Migration from Exchange API v1](https://docs.changelly.com/migration-guide)\n- https://docs.changelly.com/\n- Introduction\n\n# Introduction\nThe following methods are used to empower your service with Changelly exchange features. You can request more features by contacting our development team. Changelly API is a white-label exchange solution.\nChangelly API v2 is a faster, safer and more flexible version of our API.\nRates and limits received from the API v2 estimation methods are compatible only with API v2 and with such methods as [createTransaction](https://docs.changelly.com/float/create-transaction) and [createFixTransaction](https://docs.changelly.com/fix/create-fix-transaction). You can\'t use the rate received by one version of API to create a transaction with another one.\n\n## How to get started[\342\200\213](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#how-to-get-started)\n[\342\200\213](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#how-to-get-started)\nBefore start, follow these steps:\n1. Read the following documentation\n2. [Generate API keys](https://docs.changelly.com/development/generate-keys)\n3. Register on [the Changelly website](https://changelly.com/) if you don\'t have an account yet\n4. Contact us at [[email\302\240protected]](https://docs.changelly.com/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#3f4f4d507f5c575e51585a535346115c5052) to register your:\n[Generate API keys](https://docs.changelly.com/development/generate-keys)\n[the Changelly website](https://changelly.com/)\n[[email\302\240protected]](https://docs.changelly.com/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#3f4f4d507f5c575e51585a535346115c5052)\n- E-mail address connected to your account\n- Public API key\n- Public API key Base64\nIf you have any questions, please write us at [[email\302\240protected]](https://docs.changelly.com/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#6a1a18052a09020b040d0f06061344090507).\n- For the currencies with multiple outputs in a transaction (BTC, LTC, etc), we do not accept more than one output per address in one transaction.\n- You should integrate our API on the backend side. If you try to handle that on the frontend side, your API key will be accessible to all users.\n- It is not necessary to use Node.js for your backend. Any other server language is suitable.\n\n## Your API Extra Fee[\342\200\213](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#your-api-extra-fee)\n[\342\200\213](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#your-api-extra-fee)\nAfter setting up an API key, you may want to set up your API extra fee. For example, you may choose to charge a 0.5% fee on top of Changelly exchange fee. To set up an extra commission, please write your dedicated account manager or email us at (mailto:pro@changelly.com) with a link to your service. The [getTransactions](https://docs.changelly.com/info/get-transactions) response includes your API extra commission in percent.\n[NextUsage](https://docs.changelly.com/category/usage)\n- [How to get started](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#how-to-get-started)\n- [Your API Extra Fee](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#your-api-extra-fee)\n[How to get started](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#how-to-get-started)\n[Your API Extra Fee](https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/#your-api-extra-fee)"
        }
      }
      summary: "The following methods are used to empower your service with Changelly exchange features."
    }
    resolved_url: "https://docs.changelly.com/api-introduction/"
    latency_ms: 596
  }
}
